# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
# Anchored to the repository root: an unanchored "build/" also matches ingest/build/,
# which is source code. Same reasoning as /data/ below.
/build/
/dist/
/wheels/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tool and test caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytype/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go
#
# The launch scripts keep Go's build and module caches inside the checkout
# (GOCACHE and GOPATH), at the root or under cli/. Binaries are built, never tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gocache/
.gopath/
/cli/bin/
*.exe

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never commit credentials; use the environment.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Datasets and derived artefacts.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash: an unanchored "data/" also matches models/data/,
# which is source code. This tree holds tens of gigabytes of captures, flow
# tables, embeddings, latents and checkpoints, all of which are regenerated by
# the pipeline and none of which belongs in version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/
/references/

# Hugging Face staging. Everything under huggingface/ is uploaded as-is, so the folder holds
# only release files: handler.py, inference.py, config.json, requirements.txt, the two cards and
# the LFS rules. Those are source and are tracked, because a clone has to be able to deploy.
# Maintainer instructions live in docs/PUBLISHING.md and are deliberately NOT in this folder.
#
# What staging puts here is ignored: weights and data tables are release artefacts, regenerated
# by tools/publish/huggingface.py, and a consumer takes them from Hugging Face, not from git.
#
# `*.config.json` matches the per-stage configs the converter writes (detector.config.json and
# friends) and deliberately does NOT match the hand-written model/config.json beside them.
/huggingface/model/*.safetensors
/huggingface/model/*.config.json
/huggingface/model/*.pt
/huggingface/model/*.bin
/huggingface/dataset/processed/
/huggingface/dataset/model/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model artefacts and large binaries, wherever they appear.
# Checkpoints are outputs: the runbook regenerates every one of them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.npy
*.npz
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.feather
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# SQLite's write-ahead log and its index, beside a live database
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Captures and archives
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.7z

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run output: logs, profiles, process files, experiment trackers.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.out
*.err
*.pid
*.prof
*.lprof
nohup.out
progress.json
wandb/
runs/
lightning_logs/
mlruns/
outputs/
scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working notes, not interface documentation.
#
# Tracked deliberately: docs/*.json (machine-readable contracts -- tools/verify_contracts.py
# reads them, so a fresh clone cannot be verified without them), plus design.md,
# CODE_MAP.md, DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md, data-reference.md and the test records.
#
# Ignored below: dated status snapshots, which go stale and duplicate what git
# history already records.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/STATUS_*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test suite, kept local.
#
# The workflow guards the pytest step on `tests/` existing, so it runs here and
# is skipped on a clone. The module self-checks, the contract verifier and the
# entry-point sweep live in the source files, so CI still has something to fail
# on. Remove this line to publish the suite.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tests/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Block 10 proxy, kept local.
#
# It stands in for the real world model: it exists to settle design questions
# cheaply and its numbers are measured on slices, so publishing it alongside the
# shipped stages would misrepresent what it is.
#
# The four tools below are ignored with it because they import it directly
# (`from models.world_model_proxy.model import ...`). Tracking them without the
# package would leave a clone that fails on import.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
models/world_model_proxy/
tools/world_model/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development-only documentation: current status, the team's JSON contracts,
# experiment records and per-person guides. Kept locally, never published.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/dev/
/docs/diagrams/src/node_modules/

# every model the project serves or publishes: promoted runs, Hugging Face staging and downloads
/artifacts/
